      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white">How to Find an Exponential Function from Two Points</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          Given any two coordinate points <strong>(x₁, y₁)</strong> and <strong>(x₂, y₂)</strong> lying on the curve of <em>f(x) = a · bˣ</em>, we can solve for the unknown parameters <em>a</em> and <em>b</em> algebraically:
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4 space-y-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/80 p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60 font-mono text-xs text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
          <p><strong>Step 1: Write the system of equations</strong></p>
          <div class="pl-4 border-l-2 border-blue-500 space-y-1">
            <p>y₁ = a · b^(x₁)</p>
            <p>y₂ = a · b^(x₂)</p>
          </div>

          <p><strong>Step 2: Eliminate parameter 'a' by dividing equation 1 by equation 2</strong></p>
          <div class="pl-4 border-l-2 border-blue-500 space-y-1">
            <p>y₁ / y₂ = (a · b^(x₁)) / (a · b^(x₂))</p>
            <p>y₁ / y₂ = b^(x₁ − x₂)</p>
          </div>

          <p><strong>Step 3: Solve for the base 'b' by taking the (x₁ − x₂) root</strong></p>
          <div class="pl-4 border-l-2 border-blue-500 space-y-1">
            <p class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-bold">b = (y₁ / y₂)^(1 / (x₁ − x₂))</p>
          </div>

          <p><strong>Step 4: Substitute 'b' into equation 1 to isolate initial value 'a'</strong></p>
          <div class="pl-4 border-l-2 border-blue-500 space-y-1">
            <p class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-bold">a = y₁ / b^(x₁)</p>
          </div>

          <p><strong>Step 5: Verify against point 2</strong></p>
          <div class="pl-4 border-l-2 border-blue-500 space-y-1">
            <p>Check that a · b^(x₂) = y₂.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Exponential Growth vs. Exponential Decay</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/50 p-5 dark:border-blue-900/50 dark:bg-blue-950/20">
